lexreq:gender-06 a lexreq:Requirement ;
    skos:inScheme lexreq: ;
    lexreq:framework lexreq:GenderD32 ;
    lexreq:sortKey "4-06" ;
    rdfs:label "D3.2 §6 - CERTAIN’s Ethical Guidelines (Gender Balance)"@en ;
    lexreq:section "D3.2 §6" ;
    dcterms:source "D3.2 §6 - CERTAIN’s Ethical Guidelines (Gender Balance)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://certain-project.eu/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/CERTAIN_WP3_D3.2_Ethical-considerations-of-AI-compliance_V1.0-delivered.pdf> ;
    dcterms:description "AI practices that are gender-sensitive are highlighted through gender impact assessments, which take on defined measures and scenario-based assessments. Gender balance is achieved with regard to data sets, team composition, and evaluation. Gender audit processes are established as part of project governance. Transparency and explainability are paramount when providing information about AI systems, their purpose, capabilities, and limitations. Accordingly, explanatory processes for decision-making are made explainable to users and auditors, inclusive of establishing and maintaining records as part of the expectations for an AI model deployment, inclusive of the data sets, models, and design choices.\nAll of these guidelines will be systematically integrated into the project and examined through the creation of self-assessment tools, ensuring that ethical, fair, and gender-sensitive practices are continuously monitored and evaluated throughout the AI system’s lifecycle."@en ;
    lexreq:normativeSource "EU Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI / ALTAI - directly shape fairness, human oversight, transparency, data governance, accountability, and lifecycle monitoring."@en ;
    lexreq:normativeSource "OECD AI Principles; UNESCO Recommendation on the Ethics of AI - extend the section toward human rights, inclusion, accessibility, and societal well-being."@en ;
    lexreq:normativeSource "SGIA / gender audit approach; Horizon Europe ethics appraisal logic - ground the gender-specific operationalisation, evidence requirements, and review discipline."@en ;
    lexreq:usesTerm aidoc:AIModel , aidoc:AISystem , aidoc:Dataset , aidoc:HumanOversightMechanism , aidoc:ModelEvaluation , aidoc:TransparencyMeasure , aidoc:hasHumanOversight , aidoc:hasPerformanceMetric , aidoc:hasSourceDataset , aidoc:hasTechnicalDocumentation , aidoc:hasTransparencyMeasure , dpv:Policy , aidoc-lex:GenderImpactAssessment , aidoc-lex:GenderAudit , aidoc-lex:Procedure ;
