lexreq:gender-07 a lexreq:Requirement ;
    skos:inScheme lexreq: ;
    lexreq:framework lexreq:GenderD32 ;
    lexreq:sortKey "4-07" ;
    rdfs:label "D3.2 §4.3 / §7.1 / §7.2 - Monitoring, Risk Register Integration, and Feedback Loop"@en ;
    lexreq:section "D3.2 §4.3 / §7.1 / §7.2" ;
    dcterms:source "D3.2 §4.3 / §7.1 / §7.2 - Monitoring, Risk Register Integration, and Feedback Loop" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://certain-project.eu/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/CERTAIN_WP3_D3.2_Ethical-considerations-of-AI-compliance_V1.0-delivered.pdf> ;
    dcterms:description "Monitoring refers to the ongoing and systematic process of ensuring that managed ethical risks and gender-related risks do not compromise the AI system throughout its lifecycle. Risk identification and recording begin the process, but monitoring keeps risks visible, measurable, and manageable throughout the system's life as it is actually implemented and transformed in real-world contexts.\nIn practice, monitoring comprises a number of related activities. These activities include performing regular reviews of risks to reconsider all previously identified risks on a regular (e.g., quarterly) basis to determine whether the likelihood or severity has changed or to assess the efficacy of mitigation efforts. Monitoring also entails conducting ongoing impact assessments to review the outputs of the system and any decision-making patterns to identify any unintended ethical or gender impacts (e.g., emergent biases or disparities in users). Monitoring involves the implementation of clear and transparent means for feedback and reporting of incidents that users, stakeholders, and staff can easily access to report concerns, errors, and harms that relate to the operation of the system.\nOutputs from the self-assessment feed directly into the project’s risk register, ensuring that ethical and gender-related risks are tied to documented mitigation strategies and accountability pathways."@en ;
    lexreq:normativeSource "EU Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI / ALTAI - concretely shape accountability, monitoring, transparency, redress, and continuous improvement."@en ;
    lexreq:normativeSource "OECD AI Principles; UNESCO Recommendation on the Ethics of AI - reinforce accessible feedback channels, inclusion, and long-term societal and gender impacts."@en ;
    lexreq:normativeSource "Horizon Europe ethics appraisal logic; SGIA / gender audit approach - reinforce evidence retention, follow-up on gendered harms, and iteration from findings into mitigation and system updates."@en ;
    lexreq:usesTerm aidoc:AISystem , aidoc:HumanOversightMechanism , aidoc:PerformanceMetric , aidoc:PostMarketMonitoringActivity , aidoc:PostMarketPerformanceEvaluationActivity , aidoc:hasFrequency , aidoc:hasRisk , aidoc:hasStakeholder , aidoc-lex:IncidentReport , aidoc-lex:GenderImpactAssessment , aidoc-lex:Procedure , aidoc-lex:FeedbackLoopRisk ;
    lexreq:expectedEvidence "Incident reporting workflow"@en ;
